# Gita / VERSE//MODE — Project Intelligence

## Overview
`Gita` is the product monorepo. Cursor agents must treat this root as the workspace — not a nested kit folder as the deploy root.

## Required reads (every task)
1. `memory-bank/architecture.md`
2. `memory-bank/folder-structure.md`
3. `memory-bank/decisions.md`
4. For commerce work: `apps/web/START_HERE_CURSOR.md` and `apps/web/docs/**` as needed

## Layout (do not flatten)
- `apps/web` — Railway-deployable Next.js commerce + worker
- `services/gpu-inference` — GPU HTTP API (wraps vendors)
- `vendor/diffusers`, `vendor/fashn-vton-1.5` — upstream submodules only
- `kits/verse-mode-cursor` — non-deploy Cursor kit pointer
- `memory-bank/` — living decisions and conventions
- `infra/railway/` — deploy wiring

## Hard rules
- Never set Railway rootDirectory to `kits/` or `vendor/`.
- Never run heavy GPU inference inside the Next.js Railway web container.
- Never import `vendor/*` from Node `apps/web` — call the GPU service over HTTP.
- Preserve feature-first / layered patterns inside `apps/web` (controller → service → repository for new modules).
- Update `memory-bank/` when making cross-cutting structural decisions.

## Stack lock
Next.js 15 + React 19 + Prisma/Postgres + Auth.js + BullMQ/Redis + Zod.  
ScriptAssist (Bun/Mantine/RR7/Orval) stack does **not** apply unless an explicit migration is approved.

## Naming
See `memory-bank/folder-structure.md`. Prefer kebab-case paths, PascalCase React components.
